Five rows are inserted in each table (1 mark per table). The values must respect the types and sizes (a `PlayerID` of 6 characters, a `ClubID` of at most 10, a date in a valid format) and be consistent between the tables: every `Player.ClubID` exists in `Club`, every `Club.CoachID` exists in `Coach`, and `Coach.ClubID` points back to the club the coach manages. The data below are examples; they were inserted in SQLite and read back without error.

```sql
-- Club
INSERT INTO Club VALUES ('BARCA001', 'BARC001', 'Spain',   27, '1899-11-29');
INSERT INTO Club VALUES ('CHELS001', 'CHEL001', 'England',  6, '1905-03-10');
INSERT INTO Club VALUES ('MANCU001', 'MANC001', 'England',  9, '1880-01-01');
INSERT INTO Club VALUES ('JUVEN001', 'JUVE001', 'Italy',   36, '1897-11-01');
INSERT INTO Club VALUES ('REALM001', 'REAL001', 'Spain',   36, '1902-03-06');

-- Coach
INSERT INTO Coach VALUES ('BARC001', 'BARCA001', 'Marco Silva',   8, 'Portuguese', 52);
INSERT INTO Coach VALUES ('CHEL001', 'CHELS001', 'John Carter',   5, 'English',    48);
INSERT INTO Coach VALUES ('MANC001', 'MANCU001', 'Pierre Dubois', 11, 'French',    55);
INSERT INTO Coach VALUES ('JUVE001', 'JUVEN001', 'Luca Rossi',    7, 'Italian',    50);
INSERT INTO Coach VALUES ('REAL001', 'REALM001', 'Carlos Ruiz',   10, 'Spanish',   58);

-- Player
INSERT INTO Player VALUES ('21A001', 'BARCA001', 'Diego Alvarez', 9,  75, 120);
INSERT INTO Player VALUES ('21A002', 'CHELS001', 'Samuel Okoro',  7,  95, 110);
INSERT INTO Player VALUES ('21B001', 'MANCU001', 'Tom Baker',     10, 60, 105);
INSERT INTO Player VALUES ('21B002', 'JUVEN001', 'Paolo Neri',    4,  79, 100);
INSERT INTO Player VALUES ('21C001', 'REALM001', 'Ahmed Said',    11, 50, 130);
```

The rows are made permanent by saving the database (or by `COMMIT;` in a RDBMS that works inside transactions). Dates are entered in the format the RDBMS expects (`YYYY-MM-DD` here); they are displayed as Day/Month/Year if that display format is set on the `YearCreation` field.
